{
  "comment": "Cross-language behavioral contract for parsing video_sprites.txt sprite metadata and deciding whether a sprite may play as a video timeline. Consumed by BOTH the Kotlin suite (SpriteMetadataParityFixturesTest, driving SpriteSheetMetadata in :trailblaze-capture) and the bun suite (run-report-sprites.test.ts, driving run-report-sprites.ts). constants pins the acceptance thresholds: each suite asserts its implementation's actual constants equal these values, so a threshold can't drift in one language. parsed=null means the file must fail to parse. frameMapSamples are checked against the RESOLVED map (explicit frameMap, or identity when frameMapExplicit=false). rejection is one of multiSheet | degenerate | restampedDominated | null (accepted). To change a rule: update both implementations AND this fixture in the same change. sheetRowsSamples (optional) pin each sheet image's row count (full grids except the last sheet). rejectionMultiSheetCapable (optional) is the verdict for a consumer that declared multi-sheet support; when absent it equals rejection.",
  "constants": {
    "MIN_USEFUL_UNIQUE_FRAMES": 8,
    "MIN_ALIASING_TOTAL_FRAMES": 60,
    "RESTAMPED_SINGLE_FRAME_DOMINANCE_FRAC": 0.4
  },
